AEL — the technical blueprint

1

Context reader
Reads the shared context (our target SME, quality criteria, and scope).

Add
Gathers and imports raw sources and documents.

Appraise
Critically evaluates each added source against our quality criteria.

Translate
Translates the approved source insights into the specified language.

Draft
Generates a first draft of the handbook page based on the critically evaluated sources.

Check
Strictly checks the draft for factual accuracy, source references, and other criteria from the PRD.

Publish
Formats and publishes the approved page definitively to the shared handbook repository.

2

Architectural Design: Pipeline & Contracts (Shape 6)
Our platform uses a pipeline approach where each stage takes a file and produces a file. This file serves as the contract between parts, allowing team members to build stages simultaneously.

Seam & Contract Definition
The Seam: The handoff between the Appraise part and the Draft part.

File Name: appraised_source.json

File Shape:

JSON
{
  "source_id": "string",
  "author_or_organisation": "string",
  "reliability_justification": "string (1 line)",
  "key_findings": ["list of strings"],
  "company_relevance": "string"
}
